 ## Background
-Photometric optimization for volume rendering was introduced in the context of volume stylization and property manipulation. The method was proposed by [S1] for static volume stylization using a painting metaphor, allowing users to modify albedo, emission, and extinction to match target images. It has since been applied to various domains, including cloud synthesis [S4], egocentric view synthesis [S2], dynamic scene representation [S5], and inverse rendering [S3]. It is used for adding imprinted logos to smoke volumes, modifying volcano smoke appearance, and reconstructing extinction for refractive volumes [S1].
